    level: 'Intermediate',
    a: "Route 53 is AWS's DNS service, where I create hosted zones and records, and it can also register domains and run health checks. Routing policies include simple, weighted (split traffic by percentage), latency-based, failover (primary/secondary with health checks), geolocation and geoproximity. I use alias records to point a domain at CloudFront or an ALB, and weighted records for canary releases, like sending 10% to a new version.",
