    q: "What is ElastiCache and how do you use it?",
    level: 'Intermediate',
    a: "ElastiCache is managed in-memory caching with Redis/Valkey or Memcached, giving sub-millisecond reads. I mostly use the cache-aside pattern: read from the cache first, on a miss load from the database and store it with a TTL. That takes load off RDS for hot data like product pages and sessions. I always set a TTL so stale data eventually expires.",
    code: "import json, redis\n\nr = redis.Redis(host=\"my-cache.abc123.ng.0001.use1.cache.amazonaws.com\",\n                port=6379, ssl=True, decode_responses=True)\n\ndef get_product(product_id, db):\n    key = f\"product:{product_id}\"\n    cached = r.get(key)\n    if cached:                                   # cache hit\n        print(\"cache hit \", key)\n        return json.loads(cached)\n    print(\"cache miss\", key, \"-> reading RDS\")\n    product = db.fetch_product(product_id)       # slow path\n    r.setex(key, 300, json.dumps(product))       # keep for 5 minutes\n    return product\n\nget_product(7, db)\nget_product(7, db)",
