    q: "What is the difference between SQS, SNS and EventBridge?",
    level: 'Intermediate',
    a: "SQS is a queue: producers send messages and one consumer group pulls and processes them, which decouples services and absorbs traffic spikes. SNS is pub/sub: one message is pushed to many subscribers like SQS queues, Lambda or email. EventBridge is an event bus that routes events by content-based rules, and also handles schedules and events from AWS services and SaaS apps. With SQS and Lambda I enable partial batch responses and a dead-letter queue, so one bad message doesn't make the whole batch retry forever.",
    code: "import json\n\n# SQS -> Lambda with ReportBatchItemFailures enabled\ndef lambda_handler(event, context):\n    failures = []\n    for record in event[\"Records\"]:\n        try:\n            order = json.loads(record[\"body\"])\n            if order[\"qty\"] <= 0:\n                raise ValueError(\"bad quantity\")\n            print(\"processed order\", order[\"id\"])\n        except Exception as err:\n            print(\"failed\", record[\"messageId\"], err)\n            # only this message goes back to the queue\n            failures.append({\"itemIdentifier\": record[\"messageId\"]})\n    return {\"batchItemFailures\": failures}",
