    a: "CloudWatch is AWS's monitoring service. Metrics are numbers over time like CPUUtilization or Lambda Errors, Logs collect output from Lambda, ECS and agents, and Alarms watch a metric and fire actions like an SNS email or an Auto Scaling policy when a threshold is crossed. I always set log group retention, because the default is never expire, and I use Logs Insights to search errors quickly.",
    code: "# Email me if the API Lambda has errors 2 minutes in a row\naws cloudwatch put-metric-alarm --alarm-name orders-api-errors \\\n    --namespace AWS/Lambda --metric-name Errors \\\n    --dimensions Name=FunctionName,Value=orders-api \\\n    --statistic Sum --period 60 --evaluation-periods 2 \\\n    --threshold 1 --comparison-operator GreaterThanOrEqualToThreshold \\\n    --alarm-actions arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:123456789012:ops-alerts\n\n# Don't keep logs forever\naws logs put-retention-policy --log-group-name /aws/lambda/orders-api \\\n    --retention-in-days 30\n\naws cloudwatch describe-alarms --alarm-names orders-api-errors \\\n    --query 'MetricAlarms[].{Name:AlarmName,State:StateValue,Metric:MetricName}' --output table",
