    a: "Both store configuration and secrets encrypted with KMS. Secrets Manager costs per secret but adds automatic rotation, for example for RDS passwords, plus cross-region replication. SSM Parameter Store is free for standard parameters and great for plain config and simple secrets as SecureString. I never put secrets in code or plain environment variables; my app reads them at startup through its IAM role and caches them.",
