    level: 'Advanced',
    a: "There are six pillars: Operational Excellence, Security, Reliability, Performance Efficiency, Cost Optimization and Sustainability. They are a checklist of best practices, like automating changes, least privilege, multi-AZ, right-sizing and turning off unused resources. I run a review in the Well-Architected Tool before a big launch, and it gives a list of high and medium risks to fix.",
    code: "# Register a workload in the Well-Architected Tool, then answer\n# the questions for each pillar in the console\naws wellarchitected create-workload \\\n    --workload-name orders-platform \\\n    --description \"Orders API and web front end\" \\\n    --environment PRODUCTION \\\n    --aws-regions us-east-1 \\\n    --review-owner platform-team@example.com \\\n    --lenses wellarchitected",
