    q: "How do you deploy a FastAPI app on AWS?",
    level: 'Advanced',
    a: "I have three common options. For spiky or low traffic I run it on Lambda behind API Gateway using Mangum, which adapts API Gateway events to ASGI. For steady traffic, long requests or WebSockets I build a Docker image, push it to ECR and run it on ECS Fargate behind an ALB with uvicorn. EC2 with an Auto Scaling group is the third option when I need full control of the server. For Lambda I install dependencies for the Linux platform, because packages like pydantic-core have compiled code.",
    code: "# main.py\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom mangum import Mangum\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/items/{item_id}\")\ndef read_item(item_id: int):\n    return {\"item_id\": item_id, \"source\": \"lambda\"}\n\nhandler = Mangum(app)   # Lambda handler setting: main.handler\n\n# Package for Lambda's Linux runtime and deploy\n# pip install -r requirements.txt -t package/ \\\n#     --platform manylinux2014_x86_64 --only-binary=:all:\n# cp main.py package/ && (cd package && zip -r ../app.zip .)\n# aws lambda update-function-code --function-name fastapi-app \\\n#     --zip-file fileb://app.zip",
