    q: "How do you optimize costs on AWS?",
    level: 'Advanced',
    a: "I start with visibility: Cost Explorer, budgets and cost allocation tags per team or project. Then the big wins are right-sizing with Compute Optimizer, Savings Plans for the steady baseline, Spot for batch work, Graviton instances, S3 lifecycle rules, and turning off dev environments at night. I also regularly hunt for waste like unattached EBS volumes, old snapshots, idle load balancers, unused Elastic IPs and NAT Gateway data charges that a VPC endpoint could remove.",
    code: "# Find EBS volumes that are not attached to anything (paying for nothing)\naws ec2 describe-volumes \\\n    --filters Name=status,Values=available \\\n    --query 'Volumes[].{Id:VolumeId,GiB:Size,Type:VolumeType,Created:CreateTime}' \\\n    --output table\n\n# After checking it's not needed: snapshot (optional) and delete\naws ec2 delete-volume --volume-id vol-0aaa111bbb222ccc3",
